    <j.3:title>Towards Building Open Knowledge Base From Programming Question-Answering Communities</j.3:title>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#InformationObject"/>
    <j.2:abstract>In this paper, we propose the rst system, so-called Open Programming Knowledge Extraction (OPKE), to automatically extract knowledge from programming Question-Answering (QA) communities. OPKE is the rst step of building a programming-centric knowledge base. Data mining and Natural Language Processing techniques are leveraged to identify paraphrased questions and construct structured information. Preliminary evaluation shows the eectiveness of OPKE.</j.2:abstract>
