  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/scholarlydata/inproceedings/iswc2016/paper/posterdemo/poster-49">
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Materialization</j.3:keyword>
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SERVICE</j.3:keyword>
    <j.3:title>Proactive Replication of Dynamic Linked Data for Scalable RDF Stream Processing</j.3:title>
    <j.3:hasAuthorList rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/scholarlydata/inproceedings/iswc2016/paper/posterdemo/poster-49/authorList"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/jooik-jung"/>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SPARQL Endpoint</dc:subject>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RDF stream processing</dc:subject>
    <j.3:abstract>In this paper, we propose a proactive replication of Linked Data for RDF Stream Processing. Our solution achieves a fast query processing by replicating subsets of remote RDF datasets before query evaluation. To construct the replication process effectively, we present an update estimation model to handle the changes in updates over time. With the update estimation model, we re-compose instances of the replication process in response to some problems, i.e., the outdated data.
Finally, we conduct exhaustive tests with a real-world dataset to verify
our solution.</j.3:abstract>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#SocialObject"/>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Materialization</dc:subject>
    <j.3:isPartOf rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/conference/iswc/2016/proceedings"/>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Replication</dc:subject>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/ontology/conference-ontology.owl#InProceedings"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/sejin-chun"/>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/seungjun-yoon"/>
    <rdfs:label>Proactive Replication of Dynamic Linked Data for Scalable RDF Stream Processing</rdfs:label>
    <j.9:authorList rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/scholarlydata/inproceedings/iswc2016/paper/posterdemo/poster-49/authorList"/>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/sejin-chun"/>
    <dc:title>Proactive Replication of Dynamic Linked Data for Scalable RDF Stream Processing</dc:title>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/xiongnan-jin"/>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SERVICE</dc:subject>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#InformationObject"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/kyong-ho-lee"/>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/xiongnan-jin"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/seungjun-yoon"/>
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RDF stream processing</j.3:keyword>
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SPARQL Endpoint</j.3:keyword>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#Object"/>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/jooik-jung"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.semanticweb.org/conference/iswc/2016/paper/posterdemo/poster-49"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/spar/fabio/ProceedingsPaper"/>
    <j.2:abstract>In this paper, we propose a proactive replication of Linked Data for RDF Stream Processing. Our solution achieves a fast query processing by replicating subsets of remote RDF datasets before query evaluation. To construct the replication process effectively, we present an update estimation model to handle the changes in updates over time. With the update estimation model, we re-compose instances of the replication process in response to some problems, i.e., the outdated data.
Finally, we conduct exhaustive tests with a real-world dataset to verify
our solution.</j.2:abstract>
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Replication</j.3:keyword>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/kyong-ho-lee"/>
