  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/scholarlydata/inproceedings/iswc2016/paper/posterdemo/demo-67">
    <j.3:hasAuthorList rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/scholarlydata/inproceedings/iswc2016/paper/posterdemo/demo-67/authorList"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#SocialObject"/>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SPARQL</dc:subject>
    <j.9:authorList rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/scholarlydata/inproceedings/iswc2016/paper/posterdemo/demo-67/authorList"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/spar/fabio/ProceedingsPaper"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/giuseppe-pirro"/>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/giuseppe-pirro"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#InformationObject"/>
    <j.3:title>Gize: A Time Warp in the Web of Data</j.3:title>
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LTL</j.3:keyword>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Historical Data</dc:subject>
    <j.3:isPartOf rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/conference/iswc/2016/proceedings"/>
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SPARQL</j.3:keyword>
    <j.3:abstract>We introduce the Gize framework for querying historical RDF data. Gize builds upon two main pillars: a lightweight approach to keep historical data, and an extension of SPARQL called SPARQ–LTL, which incorporates temporal logic primitives to enable a rich class of queries. One striking point of Gize is that its features can be readily made available in existing query processors.</j.3:abstract>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/valeria-fionda"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LTL</dc:subject>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/valeria-fionda"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/ontology/conference-ontology.owl#InProceedings"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.semanticweb.org/conference/iswc/2016/paper/posterdemo/demo-67"/>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/melisachew-wudage-chekol"/>
    <rdfs:label>Gize: A Time Warp in the Web of Data</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#Object"/>
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Historical Data</j.3:keyword>
    <j.2:abstract>We introduce the Gize framework for querying historical RDF data. Gize builds upon two main pillars: a lightweight approach to keep historical data, and an extension of SPARQL called SPARQ–LTL, which incorporates temporal logic primitives to enable a rich class of queries. One striking point of Gize is that its features can be readily made available in existing query processors.</j.2:abstract>
    <dc:title>Gize: A Time Warp in the Web of Data</dc:title>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/melisachew-wudage-chekol"/>
  </rdf:Description>
