  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/scholarlydata/inproceedings/iswc2016/paper/posterdemo/demo-65">
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/stefano-faralli"/>
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Open Information Extraction</j.3:keyword>
    <j.3:hasAuthorList rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/scholarlydata/inproceedings/iswc2016/paper/posterdemo/demo-65/authorList"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#SocialObject"/>
    <j.3:title>Who-Does-What: A knowledge base of people's occupations and job activities</j.3:title>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/simone-paolo-ponzetto"/>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/jonas-bulegon-gassen"/>
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">knowledge base induction from text</j.3:keyword>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Knowledge acquisition</dc:subject>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/spar/fabio/ProceedingsPaper"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/stefano-faralli"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#InformationObject"/>
    <j.3:abstract>System analysis and design is concerned with the creation of conceptual models. In this paper, we introduce a novel resource called "Who-Does-What" (WDW) that supports the creation and quality assurance of such models. WDW provides a knowledge base of activities for classes of people engaged in a wide range of different occupations. The resource is semi-automatically created by populating the manually-created Standard Occupational Classification (SOC) of the US Department of Labor with activities found on the Web.</j.3:abstract>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/jan-mendling"/>
    <j.3:keyword rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Knowledge acquisition</j.3:keyword>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/simone-paolo-ponzetto"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/jonas-bulegon-gassen"/>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Open Information Extraction</dc:subject>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/jan-mendling"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.semanticweb.org/conference/iswc/2016/paper/posterdemo/demo-65"/>
    <j.2:abstract>System analysis and design is concerned with the creation of conceptual models. In this paper, we introduce a novel resource called "Who-Does-What" (WDW) that supports the creation and quality assurance of such models. WDW provides a knowledge base of activities for classes of people engaged in a wide range of different occupations. The resource is semi-automatically created by populating the manually-created Standard Occupational Classification (SOC) of the US Department of Labor with activities found on the Web.</j.2:abstract>
    <j.3:isPartOf rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/conference/iswc/2016/proceedings"/>
    <dc:title>Who-Does-What: A knowledge base of people's occupations and job activities</dc:title>
    <dc:subject rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">knowledge base induction from text</dc:subject>
