    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/spar/fabio/ProceedingsPaper"/>
    <j.13:maker rdf:resource="http://www.scholarlydata.org/person/manuel-atencia"/>
    <j.2:abstract>Alignments between ontologies usually come with numerical attributes expressing the confidence of each correspondence. Semantics supporting such confidences must generalise the semantics of alignments without confidence. There exists a semantics which satisfies this but introduces a discontinuity between weighted and non-weighted interpretations. Moreover, it does not provide a calculus for reasoning with weighted ontology alignments. This paper introduces a calculus for such alignments. It is given by an infinite relation-type algebra, the elements of which are weighted taxonomic relations. In addition, it approximates the non-weighted case in a continuous manner.</j.2:abstract>
